boolean     function value type
string      function value type
float       function value type
integer     function value type
bool        boolean | function value type
flo         float   | function value type
int         integer | function value type
str         string  | function value type

fget        get function from other file, must have "as" for alias, e.g. `fget filr:foo as bar;`
mov         copy value
sto         initialize/store
lod         load another file / import / module load 
add         add
sub         subtract
mul         multiply
div         divide
xor         exclusive or
cal         call
ret         return
mdf         modify (if it was used/defined before)
mod         modulo 
fgt         forget what's already lod/sto'd / delete / clean
ext         clean and exit, to forget all stuff
run         run another file or other file's functions, have to lod it first
mem         memorize, all memory is private unless `g mem value`
exp         export
err         error output
pm          pointer movement
prb         pointer remember
eq          equal
lt          less-than
gt          greater-than
nr          not required
if          conditional branch
or          or
g           global [all the things made will automatically be private unless there's g]
*           comment
** **       multi-line comment
""          unnamed
''          unnamed
!           is not
;           endline
:           unnamed | function value type
::          function value 

[p]         pointer
    new[p]      new pointer
    pos[p]      get pointer position
    val[p]      value of cell at pointer position
    run[p]      run pointer code
    rem[p]      remove pointer

notes:
    * whether a function is `global` or `private` is based on what's the allowlist on the file.
    * `run` can be runnning another file, or running a function, but you can not use run. like `foo;` would run the `def foo{}`